# Qutra Labs does not require any environment variables for local development.
# Cloud AI providers are configured at runtime inside the app (Settings > AI providers)
# and credentials are stored in the OS-backed credential store, never in .env files.

# Optional: port for Vite's dev server, Playwright, and `npm run gate`.
# Default 5174. strictPort stays true, so a taken port fails instead of hopping.
# The gate stops a listener on this port only when it is the Vite this checkout
# recorded in .qutra-dev-server.json (PID and start time); any other holder is
# left running and the gate fails.
# tauri.conf.json devUrl stays http://localhost:5174 and does not follow this.
# QUTRA_E2E_PORT=5174

# Optional: GitHub App client ID for the OAuth Device Flow (Settings > GitHub).
# This is a PUBLIC client identifier, NOT a secret — never put a client secret
# here or anywhere in the frontend/repo. Register a GitHub App with device flow
# enabled and request the minimum read-only scopes. If unset, the app offers a
# clearly-labeled fine-grained PAT dev fallback instead. Tokens are stored only
# in the OS secure store, never in .env or SQLite.
# VITE_GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=Iv1.xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
